the subtlety of art depends on the  artist's ability to deliver their  message in a single brushstroke  with 50 years of experience studying and  practicing traditional korean  calligraphy  artist hau hoyte has subtly transformed  hangul into a universal language by  blending emotion and calligraphy into a  new art form called ebiography  [Music]  [Music]  in 2005 master ha created mammography  he begins his process by finding  inspiration in nature  and also in the subtleties of korean  culture  master ha envisions which characters  he'll use to tell his story and channels  his emotions into his  [Music]  brush master hall uses hanji raging in  size often over six feet in length  using his enormous horse hair brush  master ha quickly moves from one side to  the other  creating a giant picture comprised of  lines both big and small  the messages master ha creates are  designed to read as korean letters but  subtly appear as images that can be  universally understood outside of korean  culture in this piece master hall writes  the korean word for seed looking deeper  at the piece the letters subtly  transform into a landscape with trees  and plants  each of master has works combines  letters and imagery that represent  beauty korean and western traditions and  the power of nature  without speaking master ha is able to  communicate these experiences to his  audiences as a sensual and emotional  form of art  [Music]  foreign  [Music]  you
 

